        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Riding lawn mower maintenance comes down to a short list done on schedule: oil and filters by engine hours, sharp and balanced blades, a level deck, greased fittings, even tire pressures, fresh fuel and a charged battery. None of it is difficult, and together it takes a few hours a season.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip it and the same predictable failures arrive early: gummed carburetors, worn spindles, a stretched belt mid-season and a battery that will not recover in spring. Keep a log, follow your manual's intervals over any general guide, and the machine will reward you with years of extra service.
          </p>
